  "id": "Compound::DB00734 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Risperidone is linked to Adra2c through a shared pathway involving Paliperidone, which binds to Adra2c. The evidence suggests that Risperidone causes various conditions, including Posture Abnormal, Risus Sardonicus, and Pancreatic Neoplasm, all of which are mediated by Paliperidone. These conditions are associated with an agent affecting the nervous system and an organofluorine compound, indicating a common biological mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Paliperidone in mediating the effects of Risperidone on Adra2c, suggesting a broader interaction between the drug and the receptor. The recurring association with organofluorine compounds and the nervous system suggests a possible pharmacological mechanism involving receptor binding and downstream signaling.",
